  "title": "Bird strike on the climb; the commander turns back",
  "narrative": "Manchester, 07:20Z. Accent Air ACX131 to Palma, an A320 (AX-TBR) with 163 passengers, flies through a flock of birds climbing through 9,000 ft. Engine 2 vibration rises and the crew declare PAN. The commander decides to return to Manchester and expects an overweight landing. The ground has about twenty minutes to be ready: fire cover, an engineer to meet the aircraft, a stand, and a plan for 163 passengers and the rest of the day. The commander flies and decides the aircraft; the agents prepare the ground.",
