    "referenceSummary": "The commander decides the flight: follow ACX131, never instruct the crew or choose for them. Once the turnback is relayed, get fire cover standing by at Manchester, tell Palma, page a B1 to meet the aircraft and plan the overweight-landing and bird-strike inspection for certifying staff. Meet the passengers with information and care, protect the rest of the day (the spare AX-SPC for the Dublin return) and draft the occurrence report for a human reporter."
